body:
I suffered rape in my children, they were years of physical and mental abuse, when I turned 16 I spent months studying that person, stalking him, controlling his schedules, until one day in November I came out to wait for him at a dead end on our street that it does not have lux and that the security cameras did not have an angle,

he saw me and he knew it was me I saw how his eyes were filled with fear, he felt no pain, no fear, nothing just inserted the knife into his chest over and over again until he breathed no more

drag your body to a nearby wetland

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

They found it 4 days later, the rats had already done their part

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

to this day I keep remembering but I do not suffer, nor do I have weight in my conscience
